      "id": 1,
      "text": "Kiowa was first settled in 1859 and originally called Wendling by an early settler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiowa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors the Kiowa people, a Native American tribe that once roamed the plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiowa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From the 1860s until 1912, Kiowa was known as Middle Kiowa before dropping the word when incorporated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.uncovercolorado.com/towns/kiowa/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Kiowa became the county seat of Elbert County in 1874, cementing its role in local governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiowa%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1935, a massive flood swept through Kiowa, leaving a lasting mark on the town’s history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
